    "title": "pandas.tseries.offsets.YearBegin.month — pandas 3.0.5 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.tseries.offsets.YearBegin.month#\n\n- YearBegin.month#\n- Return the month of the year on which this offset applies. Returns an integer representing the month (1-12) that this offset targets. For year-based offsets, this determines which month is used for calculations. See also \n  - `tseries.offsets.YearEnd`\n  - Offset to end of year.\n  - `tseries.offsets.YearBegin`\n  - Offset to start of year.\n  - `tseries.offsets.BYearEnd`\n  - Offset to last business day of year.\n  - `tseries.offsets.BYearBegin`\n  - Offset to first business day of year.\n Examples >>> pd.offsets.BYearBegin().month 1 >>> pd.offsets.BYearBegin(month=6).month 6",
    "markdown_length": 639,
